<!--
    Objective-C message sends to a class the image only imports, resolved and
    typed from the SDK declarations (`option objcresolve`, `option objcsdk`).

    Issue: an app reaches a Foundation class through a __got slot bound to
    `_OBJC_CLASS_$_<name>`. `objcresolve` knew only the image's own classes,
    so `[KNumber numberWithLongLong:v]` printed
    `objc_msgSend$numberWithLongLong:(&OBJC_CLASS_$_KNumber,v)`, the send to its
    result `objc_msgSend$stringValue(...)`, and an undeclared factory's result
    `[KNumber numberWithInt:7]` an untyped `unsigned long`.

    Fix: the ObjC analysis adds the classes the image imports or subclasses,
    with their superclasses, from the headers `objcsdk` names; a data import
    slot bound to a class object is a class receiver. The class send resolves
    to `+[KNumber numberWithLongLong:]`, the instance send along the superclass
    chain to `-[KValue stringValue]`, and a factory whose leading noun is the
    class's (`numberWith...` on `KNumber`) returns `KNumber *`.
    The fixture header objc_sdk_sends/KNumber.h is hand-written.

    The receiver is followed by its value: through `objc_opt_self` and the
    other runtime functions returning their argument, a value a call leaves
    alone, and a join whose inputs all name the class (`send_via_self`,
    `send_joined`).

    Pass 1 (`objcresolve off`): the runtime stubs and `unsigned long v2`.
    Pass 2 (default): the methods and `KNumber *v2`.
-->
<bytechunk space="ram" offset="0x100000" readonly="true">
c0035fd6
</bytechunk>
<symbol space="ram" offset="0x100000" name="harness_stub"/>
</binaryimage>
